  "description": "What: a man is seen by thermal at the hour the old rule hid every target (CE-1987, R-1058; docs/DESIGN_Thermal_And_Acoustic_Sensing.md \u00a79.2). On wide-corridor (52.5\u00b0N; a grass strip along y 185\u2013215) at 09:36 local \u2014 solar ~08:30, where the retired crossover proxy dimmed every passive signature to its floor (a standing man read 0.22, under the sight's 0.3) \u2014 clear sky: 'Observer' (the thermal observer, TKB 215: 4 K of contrast) at (80, 200), 'Man' (a hostile rifleman, inert, standing) on the grass at (480, 200), 400 m east. Judge: his clothing (~28 \u00b0C) is ~10 K above the morning grass, so the observer's memory holds him with the THERMAL bit. Fail: no thermal bit (only his eyes saw him). Red-proof: raise the sight's MinContrastK above his contrast and the thermal bit never comes.",
